1
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:11,420
This is Deadly Queen.

2
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,677
I bestowed it with a moniker myself. Hmph.

3
00:00:14,760 --> 00:00:17,057
I'm only telling you
because you're going to die.

4
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:20,137
After you bite the dust, I'll
be able to sleep soundly.

5
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:23,380
Hey, didn't I warn you not
to make a move against me?

6
00:00:23,580 --> 00:00:25,637
You're about to learn
that I mean business!

7
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:26,550
Yes!

8
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:32,186
Well now, color me surprised.

9
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:36,556
I crushed several of these vermin,
yet you remain completely unscathed.

10
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,517
This is your last chance, pal.

11
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,917
Move again and I'll slice whatever
that big artery is in your neck.

12
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,412
Oh yeah, now I remember.

13
00:00:43,540 --> 00:00:44,997
It's called the carotid artery.

14
00:00:45,080 --> 00:00:49,317
You move a muscle, and I'll have my
invincible harvest hack it to pieces.

15
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:51,417
Judging by the look of
that stand of yours,

16
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:54,577
it pecks a wallop if you're up close, but
it's really shitty when it comes down?

17
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:55,836
long-range fighting.

18
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:59,637
If I had to guess, I'd say it's got
a range of one, maybe two meters.

19
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:03,485
So go ahead and make your move,
if you're ready to die, that is.

20
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,430
Fascinating.

21
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:10,108
From the looks of things, it seems each
user is endowed with a unique ability.

22
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:11,870
Stand.

23
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:14,060
I believe that's the term you used.

24
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,340
I should tell you,

25
00:01:16,800 --> 00:01:21,447
as far as special abilities go, Deadly
Queen has one that puts others to shame.

26
00:01:22,180 --> 00:01:23,010
Hmm?

27
00:01:23,093 --> 00:01:24,157
What's that in its hand?

28
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:25,240
Grab it, Harvest!

29
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:28,470
That's weird.

30
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:30,542
It's just a normal 100 yen coin.

31
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,797
What the heck were you
planning to do with this?

32
00:01:32,880 --> 00:01:33,710
Simple.

33
00:01:33,793 --> 00:01:38,017
I was going to reveal what makes Deadly
Queen such a unique and terrifying stand.

34
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:42,697
There's no point in keeping its powers
secret when you're already as good as dead.

35
00:01:42,780 --> 00:01:45,020
Deadly Queen has an astonishing power.

36
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:50,320
Any object that it touches becomes an
explosive that rips its target asunder.

37
00:01:51,760 --> 00:01:56,140
That's right, even something as
simple as a hundred yen coin.

38
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:58,900
Quick harvest!

39
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,612
You have to let go of the coin right now!

40
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:13,160
That didn't take long.

41
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:15,920
Now a night of glorious sleep awaits.

42
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:41,580
Thank you.

43
00:02:57,460 --> 00:03:00,260
Thank you.

44
00:03:20,320 --> 00:03:24,620
I love you, so I love you!

45
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:51,150
Wait a second.

46
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,140
My face is...

47
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,560
What happened to me?

48
00:04:00,140 --> 00:04:01,180
I told you.

49
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:05,917
Deadly Queen has the ability to transform
anything it touches into a bomb.

50
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,937
That's what it was doing when you
asked about this hundred-yen coin.

51
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:12,937
I press the detonator whenever the
urge hits me, and once it's triggered,

52
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:15,597
my victim is blown to
smithereens from the inside out.

53
00:04:15,680 --> 00:04:17,880
Though in your case, Shigechi,

54
00:04:18,320 --> 00:04:21,457
it appears the blast partially
imploded your malformed face?

55
00:04:21,540 --> 00:04:27,080
Leaving behind a stomach-churning cocktail
of facial fascia and cerebral tissue!

56
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:30,817
Before I deliver the blow
that ends your wretched life.

57
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:33,577
There's something of great
importance I must ask you.

58
00:04:33,660 --> 00:04:36,457
Earlier you referred to
this power as a stand.

59
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:40,840
Do the others, Josuke and Okuyasu,
also wield the power of the stand?

60
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:43,680
I don't want to die
here, somebody help me,

61
00:04:46,580 --> 00:04:48,857
Your death is a necessity at this point.

62
00:04:48,940 --> 00:04:51,877
Now that you know my secret,
I can't let you live.

63
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,260
It's nothing personal,

64
00:04:53,500 --> 00:04:58,117
but I can't allow a single living soul to
know the true nature of Yoshikage Kira.

65
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:02,500
Though I must admit, I find myself
fascinated by these stand users.

66
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:04,980
I could figure this out on my own,

67
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:08,748
but I'd rather use the fleeting
resource that lies before me.

68
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:12,720
Josuke, Okuyasu, who are
the others besides them?

69
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:15,880
How many users are residing in this town?

70
00:05:17,200 --> 00:05:18,494
What are their powers?

71
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:19,950
Don't know.

72
00:05:20,033 --> 00:05:21,500
Just let me go. Please.

73
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:22,870
Come now.

74
00:05:22,953 --> 00:05:24,737
I'm sure you know more
than you're letting on.

75
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:30,260
And if you refuse to tell me, your
parents will pay for it with their lives.

76
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:33,130
What?

77
00:05:33,213 --> 00:05:34,860
No, you can't.

78
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:37,780
I won't let you hurt my mommy and daddy.

79
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:42,637
Well, I won't have to if you hurry up
and give me the answers I'm looking for.

80
00:05:42,720 --> 00:05:43,877
Now quit your stalling.

81
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:46,157
I need to slip away before anyone sees me.

82
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:47,593
Just the names will do.

83
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,682
Hop to it, boy.

84
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:50,270
Hang on.

85
00:05:50,500 --> 00:05:52,857
Everyone says there was a
murderer in this town and

86
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:55,917
they're all trying to track
him down before he kills again.

87
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,760
It's all making sense now.

88
00:05:57,980 --> 00:06:00,057
The killer they were talking about is you.

89
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:01,697
You messed up son of a bitch.

90
00:06:01,780 --> 00:06:04,240
You killed Reimi Sugimoto too. What?

91
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:05,989
How do you know that girl?

92
00:06:06,860 --> 00:06:09,213
The little shit can still use his stand?

93
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,500
This isn't good.

94
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:12,300
Deadly queen!

95
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,040
That brat.

96
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:22,800
I was so close to killing him.

97
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:33,460
I managed to give him the slip.

98
00:06:34,140 --> 00:06:36,400
Now I just have to get to Josuke.

99
00:06:38,540 --> 00:06:42,300
Once I make it there, he can use
his shining diamond to fix me.

100
00:06:43,500 --> 00:06:47,420
There's no way I'm going to
sit back and die like this.

101
00:06:51,940 --> 00:06:56,080
No matter what, I'll protect
my mommy and my daddy.

102
00:06:57,360 --> 00:07:01,780
I promise I'll fight to keep them
safe from this hand-hoarding monster.

103
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:06,540
That horrible creep is rotten to the core.

104
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:11,929
And I'd rather die than let them live
in the same town as my mommy and daddy.

105
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,860
I have to find Josuke.

106
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,680
If he heals me, I can save him.

107
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:30,220
Sorry about that.

108
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:32,999
Hey, kid, you're not hurt, are you?

109
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:35,100
I have to find him.

110
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:38,117
Gee, I wonder what's the
matter with the little guy.

111
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:41,141
I don't know, but he looks
like a middle School.

112
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:42,760
Oh, no.

113
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,497
Something's wrong with him.

114
00:07:44,580 --> 00:07:46,577
Let's see if we can find a teacher.

115
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:47,897
We should leave him be.

116
00:07:47,980 --> 00:07:49,098
He's kind of weird.

117
00:07:49,700 --> 00:07:50,530
Come on.

118
00:07:57,660 --> 00:07:58,490
Josuke!

119
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:06,870
Josuke!

120
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,294
I recall you said something
about people looking for me.

121
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:19,537
Does that mean there's
someone else here who

122
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:22,326
knows the truth about
Reimi Sugimoto's murder?

123
00:08:23,840 --> 00:08:27,016
Even if there is, they won't
be able to track me down.

124
00:08:27,920 --> 00:08:31,760
The fact remains, no one knows
Yoshikage Kira's true colors.

125
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:36,439
It's a secret you'll have to carry
with you all the way to the grave.

126
00:08:37,360 --> 00:08:38,190
No!

127
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:39,900
I'm gonna protect Mommy!

128
00:08:42,980 --> 00:08:46,862
Sorry, but Deadly Queen has already
left its mark on the doorknob.

129
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:02,840
Behold the genius of my Deadly Queen.

130
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:07,417
All evidence of my true
self has been destroyed.

131
00:09:07,500 --> 00:09:10,440
Hey, did you hear someone
call my name just now?

132
00:09:11,220 --> 00:09:12,514
Yeah, most definitely.

133
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,499
Josuke, you seeing what I'm seeing?

134
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:24,140
I got it.

135
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:28,060
No, Shigechi!

136
00:09:31,060 --> 00:09:31,890
Shigechi!

137
00:09:33,080 --> 00:09:35,317
Hey, something's not right, Josuke.

138
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:38,397
Harvest was limping around and
bleeding before it vanished,

139
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,977
but that's not how a
stand usually disappears.

140
00:09:41,060 --> 00:09:44,295
And why the heck would only
one of them come to see us?

141
00:09:49,940 --> 00:09:51,797
Let's head over to the middle school.

142
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:53,939
We have to find Shigechi right now.

143
00:09:56,980 --> 00:09:57,810
What's this?

144
00:09:58,080 --> 00:10:00,609
Where could I have
possibly lost my button?

145
00:10:01,200 --> 00:10:02,917
Well, it can't be helped.

146
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,860
I just have to visit my tailor
and hope he carries the same kind.

147
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:24,980
It can't be. Not again.

148
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,680
That foul demon.

149
00:10:28,060 --> 00:10:29,980
He's taken another life.

150
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:34,877
Another victim screams across the skies.

151
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,640
Why does this keep happening?

152
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:46,460
Shigechi

153
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:02,529
There's no doubt about it.

154
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:04,160
This boy has passed.

155
00:11:05,720 --> 00:11:07,737
Shigekio must have had a
run-in with the killer.

156
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:09,408
One that cost him his life.

157
00:11:09,620 --> 00:11:11,326
The whole thing is sickening.

158
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:13,817
I know what you must be thinking.

159
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:16,371
How did they meet and how was he murdered?

160
00:11:16,880 --> 00:11:18,057
But I have no idea.

161
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:19,940
I'm positive it was his doing.

162
00:11:20,560 --> 00:11:23,517
I'd recognize the handiwork
of that murderer anywhere.

163
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:24,430
Trust me.

164
00:11:25,540 --> 00:11:28,757
We just looked for Shigeki but
couldn't find him anywhere.

165
00:11:28,840 --> 00:11:30,937
I still don't get how
this could have happened.

166
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:33,961
We only let him out of our
sight for five minutes.

167
00:11:34,220 --> 00:11:37,357
His books and school supplies are
in the same place he left them,

168
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,837
and his parents have filed
a missing person report?

169
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:43,077
though I doubt anything useful
will turn up at this point.

170
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,200
I have to wonder.

171
00:11:44,820 --> 00:11:46,537
Wait, what are you saying, Josuke?

172
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:49,326
You don't think a stand
user did this, do you?

173
00:11:50,260 --> 00:11:54,800
You guys couldn't possibly know this,
but Shigechi's stand harvest was, well,

174
00:11:55,160 --> 00:11:56,957
in a word, the thing was
damn near invincible.

175
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:58,240
So what the hell?

176
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:00,912
This guy killed Shigechi in five minutes.

177
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:04,374
Then he hit his body off
campus without anyone noticing.

178
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,437
Well, there you have it, Jotaro.

179
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:09,717
It's pretty obvious that we're
dealing with a murderous stand user.

180
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:12,565
We can't just sit by and
watch like spectators.

181
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:13,910
Hey, Josuke.

182
00:12:14,100 --> 00:12:16,037
You said you found a button, right?

183
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:16,950
Oh, yeah.

184
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:20,061
Harvest brought it to me
before falling to pieces.

185
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,150
Here you go.

186
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:24,740
This is Shigechi's dying message.

187
00:12:25,380 --> 00:12:28,297
It's very likely Harvest
pulled it off the murderer.

188
00:12:28,380 --> 00:12:30,851
If so, we've been given an important clue.

189
00:12:31,160 --> 00:12:33,457
I'd like to investigate
this thing further.

190
00:12:33,540 --> 00:12:35,820
Mind if I keep it? Be my guest,

191
00:12:35,980 --> 00:12:39,157
but how much information can you really
get from some run-of-the-mill button?

192
00:12:39,240 --> 00:12:40,617
More than you would think.

193
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:44,524
We might find the brand of the
clothes, or even the manufacturer.

194
00:12:44,860 --> 00:12:45,690
Good idea.

195
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:50,680
Hey, if we're done with this little
meeting, I think I'm gonna go home.

196
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:54,637
Talking about all this is
putting me in a weird mood.

197
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:56,197
I'm really pissed.

198
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:59,040
Come on, dad, let's go!

199
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:01,757
What's up with him?

200
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,117
This isn't like him at all.

201
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:05,237
Yeah, but I know how he feels.

202
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:08,237
Shigeji may have come off as
an annoying greedy bastard

203
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:11,137
but there was something
undeniably lovable about him.

204
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:14,237
I still haven't wrapped my head
around the fact that he's gone.

205
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:17,477
Honestly, I'm not sure how to feel.

206
00:13:17,560 --> 00:13:21,017
I don't know whether to rage at
the world or cry my eyes out.

207
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:23,917
It's one of the most irritating
things you can imagine.

208
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,471
I'm sure he feels it too.

209
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:28,400
But it's probably way worse for him.

210
00:13:29,580 --> 00:13:30,410
Shit!

211
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:34,717
How could something so horrific be
happening in Mariah right under my nose?

212
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:39,035
I'll make sure all my customers know
to keep an eye out for this madman.

213
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:43,495
I can't imagine he would pay me a
visit, but I'll take some precautions.

214
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:47,477
Keep in mind, stand users have a
nasty habit of finding each other.

215
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:49,620
That said, I hope we never meet.

216
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:53,925
So the time has come for
us all to take action.

217
00:14:20,380 --> 00:14:21,210
Hmm?

218
00:14:21,293 --> 00:14:22,600
That was definitely Josuke.

219
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:26,900
And Okuyasu is with him.

220
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,360
You won't believe what happened.

221
00:14:29,900 --> 00:14:33,037
So you remember how it was
my birthday this past Friday?

222
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:35,537
Well, that guy I'm seeing
decided to give me a gift.

223
00:14:35,620 --> 00:14:38,977
I mean, if you can even call it
that, it's just a shitty ring.

224
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:41,617
I wouldn't be caught
dead wearing this thing.

225
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:45,477
I know, but for now I have to
be like, oh my god, I love it.

226
00:14:45,560 --> 00:14:48,397
Jeez, I'm only dating him
because his dad owns some land.

227
00:14:48,480 --> 00:14:49,717
The guy's a total hick.

228
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:52,447
I bet if this crap is
the best he can afford.

229
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:53,797
How much did it cost?

230
00:14:53,880 --> 00:14:55,760
I'm guessing like $150,000.

231
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:58,917
If you want it, I bet you
could sell it at a pawn shop.

232
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,412
I can't let my beautiful fingers
be sullied by such trash.

233
00:15:03,680 --> 00:15:06,200
Her soul is as grotesque as they come.

234
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:08,820
But her hands and face are quite lovely.

235
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:13,100
I'd like to set her soul right
and show her a glorious time.

236
00:15:13,620 --> 00:15:14,897
Well, I've got to get going.

237
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:17,200
I'll see you soon. Okay, then. Later.

238
00:15:22,860 --> 00:15:24,684
Time we went our separate ways.

239
00:15:25,020 --> 00:15:27,196
We had a good run, but it's over now.

240
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:53,180
Good morning, everyone, and
welcome to Mariah Radio.

241
00:15:53,800 --> 00:15:58,160
This is Kai Harada, your easy-listening
disc jockey extraordinaire.

242
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:00,757
Are you ready for a magnificent week?

243
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:03,077
It's hard to believe there are
only three days left to do this.

244
00:16:03,160 --> 00:16:04,420
Feel free to dig in.

245
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:07,200
Oh, I almost forgot.

246
00:16:07,360 --> 00:16:10,257
I'm going to be out of the house
today running a few errands,

247
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:12,340
so I'd like you to stay put, okay?

248
00:16:13,640 --> 00:16:15,717
We'll wine and dine when I get back.

249
00:16:15,800 --> 00:16:16,976
How does that sound?

250
00:16:23,420 --> 00:16:26,257
Thankfully, they still had some
of the Parisian specials left.

251
00:16:26,340 --> 00:16:27,717
We got here in the nick of time.

252
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:28,717
Let's head over to Yohei Lake.

253
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,880
But Asuka's not here yet. Oh, yeah.

254
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:34,906
It's been four days since we
found out about Shigechi's murder.

255
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:40,620
It's been fairly quiet since then, but...

256
00:16:43,620 --> 00:16:47,679
There's still a killer lurking
somewhere in the shadows of this town.

257
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:52,007
When it comes down to it, the
mind only sees what it wants to.

258
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:56,027
The look of guilt and innocence
is in the eye of the beholder.

259
00:17:04,260 --> 00:17:07,120
Oh, uh, hi there, Mr. Jotaro.

260
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:12,487
Did anything weird stick out to
you during your investigation?

261
00:17:13,080 --> 00:17:14,320
You remember, right?

262
00:17:14,460 --> 00:17:16,877
You said something about
examining the murderer's button?

263
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,560
Oh, that, not yet.

264
00:17:19,180 --> 00:17:20,677
Hopefully that changes soon.

265
00:17:20,760 --> 00:17:21,590
Hmm.

266
00:17:22,020 --> 00:17:23,608
Yeah, it'd be a great help.

267
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:31,460
So, um, you headed anywhere in particular?

268
00:17:34,020 --> 00:17:35,680
No, not really.

269
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:37,540
I'm just walking.

270
00:17:37,660 --> 00:17:38,600
Oh, I see.

271
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:43,340
Son of a bitch.

272
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:46,877
Getting the strong silent type
to chat is like pulling teeth.

273
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:51,842
Rohan-sensei's pushiness is unsettling,
But Jotaro's silence sends me into a panic.

274
00:17:52,160 --> 00:17:54,807
There's gotta be something
we can talk about.

275
00:17:54,980 --> 00:17:55,810
Let's see.

276
00:17:57,080 --> 00:17:59,256
I think that coat of yours is Bites!

277
00:18:01,980 --> 00:18:03,921
Looks like we found a shoe store.

278
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:05,090
Huh?

279
00:18:05,173 --> 00:18:06,003
What do you know?

280
00:18:06,086 --> 00:18:07,840
It is a shoe store. Good catch.

281
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:09,740
Uh, is something wrong?

282
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:11,670
Oh.

283
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:15,017
It is a shoe store, but they
also do simple alterations.

284
00:18:15,100 --> 00:18:16,317
Well, that's certainly convenient.

285
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:19,377
if anyone ever needs their skirt
waists and pants hemmed high,

286
00:18:19,460 --> 00:18:20,290
know where to send them.

287
00:18:20,373 --> 00:18:22,697
Plus, the electronics shop sells flowers.

288
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:24,662
What made you want to stop here?

289
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:28,217
I did a bit of digging and learned
all about the tailors of Morioh,

290
00:18:28,300 --> 00:18:31,777
but it didn't occur to me till
now to ask about places like this.

291
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:32,690
Oh.

292
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:34,810
Hmm.

293
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:41,247
So, is there something
wrong with the button?

294
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:42,210
No.

295
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:44,876
If it doesn't ring a bell, forget it.

296
00:18:45,080 --> 00:18:48,609
I just couldn't remember what
it was originally attached to.

297
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:49,740
That's too bad.

298
00:18:50,240 --> 00:18:52,197
Hey, kid, want an animal cracker?

299
00:18:52,280 --> 00:18:53,110
I got plenty.

300
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:56,777
I saved the camels for last, but
everything else is fair game,

301
00:18:56,860 --> 00:18:58,857
so feel free to take
as many as you can eat.

302
00:18:58,940 --> 00:19:01,117
Thanks, but no, I'm fine for now, sir.

303
00:19:01,200 --> 00:19:02,030
Suit yourself.

304
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:06,157
Getting back to the point,
not only have I seen it,

305
00:19:06,240 --> 00:19:08,977
believe it or not, I actually
just finished some alterations!

306
00:19:09,060 --> 00:19:10,937
on the jacket that it belongs to.

307
00:19:11,020 --> 00:19:13,777
A customer dropped by yesterday
and asked me to replace

308
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:16,860
a missing button with the
same kind you brought in.

309
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:18,380
See for yourselves.

310
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,759
They're identical.

311
00:19:20,080 --> 00:19:20,997
Does this mean…

312
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,360
It looks that way.

313
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:23,796
We found it, Koichi.

314
00:19:24,320 --> 00:19:26,460
Found what exactly? Oh, nothing.

315
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:29,517
More importantly, what did
the customer look like?

316
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:30,953
Do you recall his name?

317
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:32,180
Are you serious?

318
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:33,540
Of course I do.

319
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,857
What kind of businessman
would I be if I didn't?

320
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:40,137
Each and every one of my customers' names
is filed away in the old noggin here.

321
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:43,357
Anything less would just be rude
to my well-paying clientele.

322
00:19:43,440 --> 00:19:46,257
I've got thousands of
names locked away in here.

323
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:47,260
You don't say.

324
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:49,840
You're absolutely incredible, sir!

325
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:53,045
Would you mind telling
us who owns that jacket?

326
00:19:53,940 --> 00:19:56,999
Well, I guess helping you
out couldn't hurt nothing.

327
00:19:57,100 --> 00:19:59,159
I keep the names on the order tags.

328
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:01,900
So you know, I don't need these tags.

329
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:03,944
I remember the names just fine.

330
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:07,747
But things tend to run more
smoothly when I have them on hand.

331
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:13,540
Let's see here.

332
00:20:14,600 --> 00:20:16,180
Huh? That's interesting.

333
00:20:16,500 --> 00:20:18,297
How do you read this last name?

334
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:19,997
It has to be...

335
00:20:20,080 --> 00:20:23,417
I don't mean to rush you, sir, but
maybe I can help you figure it out?

336
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:24,900
That can't be it.

337
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:26,260
Maybe it's...

338
00:20:37,260 --> 00:20:38,090
Oh!

339
00:20:44,020 --> 00:20:46,000
Look over here. Ah!

340
00:20:46,640 --> 00:20:48,160
Why'd my hand explode?

341
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:50,365
What the hell's going on here?

342
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:53,600
Look over here. Ah! Jotaro!

343
00:20:53,880 --> 00:20:55,097
Tell me you're saying this!

344
00:20:55,180 --> 00:20:58,017
Just keep your guard up, Koichi,
and don't get any closer to it.

345
00:20:58,100 --> 00:20:59,980
Hey, didn't you hear me?

346
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:01,940
I said look over here.

347
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:15,300
Is that his stand?

348
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:21,065
Jotaro, look at the coat rack!

349
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:25,555
The killer is here, and he's
trying to take the jacket!

350
00:21:27,560 --> 00:21:30,217
I never imagined someone
would go so far as to

351
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:32,717
investigate the button
that fell off my jacket.

352
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:34,212
What a careless mistake.

353
00:21:34,320 --> 00:21:35,360
This is bad.

354
00:21:35,900 --> 00:21:38,018
Have those two already seen my name?

355
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:41,534
Why have I been faced with
nothing but adversity lately?

356
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,280
Ah, good grief.

357
00:21:43,600 --> 00:21:46,188
This would be when he
comes to get his suit.

358
00:21:46,740 --> 00:21:48,446
Panicking would be a mistake.

359
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:52,092
I'll simply execute them with
Deadly Queen's Bomb Type II.

360
00:21:52,300 --> 00:21:54,860
Just like that pathetic punk Shigechi.

361
00:21:56,580 --> 00:21:57,800
It's moving again!

362
00:21:59,100 --> 00:22:01,240
Our evidence! Wait!

363
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:03,697
We can't go blindly after it.

364
00:22:03,780 --> 00:22:06,133
Look at the way he's pulling the jacket.

365
00:22:06,440 --> 00:22:07,300
It's strange.

366
00:22:16,100 --> 00:22:17,440
What is his power?

367
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:22,848
Watch out, it's gonna blow!

368
00:23:03,780 --> 00:23:06,057
I move so slightly to
the arms and the lips and

369
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:08,417
the face of the humic and
of all that I need to.

370
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:11,197
I want to come and stand
a little bit closer.

371
00:23:11,280 --> 00:23:13,477
Breathe in and get a bit higher.

372
00:23:13,560 --> 00:23:17,957
You'll never know what
hit you when I get to you!

373
00:23:18,040 --> 00:23:22,300
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you.

374
00:23:23,060 --> 00:23:25,540
Ooh, I got it if I need you.

375
00:23:27,000 --> 00:23:31,237
Ooh, I want you, I don't
know if I need you?

376
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:34,380
But, ooh, I'm done for now.
